COMPOSITION SOLVABILITY GATE (R32) — s2/composition_gate.py
Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B, RTX 4090, 3 seeds, L=3 (2-hop), full-FT direct-gold single-step, LR=2e-5, 1000 steps
Purpose: before running grow-vs-fixed arms on cross-stream composition, verify the task is
achievable AT ALL by an upper-bound model. If even the upper bound can't compose, arms would be
0-vs-0 and must NOT be read as "growth useless".

n_chains=22  n_edges=44  (single-token non-source pool = 44)

== GATE A (mean/3 seeds), no-memory single-step-only upper bound ==
  single-step seen: A->B=1.000 B->C=1.000 | para: A->B=1.000 B->C=1.000  (knowledge fully in weights)
  2-hop A->C : seen=0.000 para=0.000 | derange-ctrl=0.000 base-untrained=0.000 goldC-prob=2.5e-8
  => GATE A FAIL (thr=0.30; need single-step(all views)>0.8 and 2hop>>control)

== GATE B (single-step knowledge present; direct 2-hop supervised on 70% train chains) ==
  [seed 0] direct-2hop train-fit=1.000 held-out=0.000
  [seed 1] direct-2hop train-fit=1.000 held-out=0.000
  [seed 2] direct-2hop train-fit=1.000 held-out=0.000
  direct-2hop: train-fit=1.000 held-out=0.000
  => GATE B: train-fits perfectly but held-out=0 -> composition operator does NOT generalize to
     new chains even with direct 2-hop supervision (OOD compositionality gap).

